# Context

## Background
A code review of 20590df (the Go rewrite) compared the new engine
against the deleted bin/looper.sh and lib/looper_parallel.py and found
nine behavioral regressions. This commit fixes all nine.

## Why This Way
- Failure classification reads only the process error plus the last
  8 KiB of the event log because the whole log contains the agent's
  session output: a timed-out test it was fixing, or a file named
  *_timeout*, used to trigger up to 12 retries with 10-minute backoff.
- The git timeout is a package-level var assigned in Parse rather than
  a Repository field because gitCommand is also called as a free
  function (for example, from the assessment path).
- The prepare-defer retry clears when a speculative check completes,
  because that is the only event that moves the chain base the next
  merge targets.

## Gotchas
- to-do.json and to-do.schema.json are gitignored runtime files; the
  matching backlog for this work lives beside the repo, untracked.
- TestShippedSchemaMatchesDefault skips when no repository-local
  to-do.schema.json exists (fresh clones); initialize writes the
  built-in default beside the task file when none exists.

